Per test: none of them failed on an assertion about behavior. Every one stopped at NotImplementedError in the contract function shown, before reaching its assertions. Two dashboard screen tests, AT01_1 and AT01_2 on the screen, are the only ones that stop in a collaborator: they fail when opening the Onboard Store, before StationScreens.dashboard is called. They will fail on dashboard once the store exists.

How the tests are built

Fixtures: test data is built only from Domain Rules types and the store write functions in the contract.
AT-03 Earth enforcement: the services are passed into EarthGateway.handle as spies. “Nothing created” means no service was reached.
Error code: every rejection asserts the error class, and that args[0] is a non-empty list of failures.
Controls: each control is the adjacent test, or the paired subtest inside the matrix.

Things the contract doesn’t fully cover

Earth dashboard: no service function serves it, so AT01_6 checks only the stored count reported_pending_count, not the S1 page.
Screen markup: the screens’ HTML isn’t in the contract, so screen assertions are text and order only. The activity entry count is checked through recent_activity instead.
Plural unit names: AT01 expects “6 / 10 packs” from the AC text while the unit is named “pack”. The spec never says how unit names become plural.
“Most recently changed”: for next_mission, this is judged by the latest status-history time, the only time field a mission has.
Earth Store connection string: the format isn’t specified, so the tests pass a sqlite:/// path.

